Ladybird’s default User-Agent string has AppleWebKit/537.36 ahead of
Chrome/153.0.0.0, which is the order that Chrome uses. Chrome’s own
BuildUserAgentFromOSAndProduct() (in user_agent_utils.cc) formats every
User-Agent string as “AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko)”, then the
product token, then Safari/537.36. And WebKit’s UserAgentGLib.cpp puts
AppleWebKit/605.1.15 at the same place, ahead of any product token.
